<title>LITHUANIA: COMMISSION BACKS $200 MLN BUTINGE CREDIT.</title>
<headline>COMMISSION BACKS $200 MLN BUTINGE CREDIT.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The foreign loans commission said on Wednesday it will suggest the government pass to parliament a draft law issuing a state guarantee to six Western banks for a $200 million credit for the planned Butinge oil terminal. </p>
<p>The European Affairs Ministry said in a statement that the draft law will include a state guarantee for credits for the construction of Butinge.</p>
<p>The statement said the state guarantee would be given to the Union Bank of Switzerland (U.S. branch), U.S EXIM Bank, Kreditanstalt fur Wiederaufbau, UBS Switzerland, the Bank of Tokyo or Mitsubishi Corp and the Nordic Investment Bank.</p>
<p>The statement also said that the total state guarantee sum may not exceed $200 million.</p>
<p>It also said the commission would suggest the government issue a one-year guarantee to Saab Aircraft for $200,000 for a leasing deal with Lithuanian Airlines for Saab 340 B aircraft.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
